{"availability":"available","full":"risingwavelabs/risingwave","name":"risingwave","description":"Event streaming platform for agentic AI. Continuously ingest, transform, and serve event streams in real time, at scale.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":9364,"forks":848,"created":"2022-01-28T12:58:03Z","updated":"2026-10-09T20:10:24Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://go.risingwave.com/slack","topics":["apache-iceberg","data-engineering","database","etl-pipeline","event-streaming","kafka","materialized-view","postgresql","rust","stream-processing","webhook"],"demo":"https://docs.risingwave.com/get-started/quickstart","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:21.675Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:21.675Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:21.675Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:21.675Z","stars":9364,"forks":848}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["RisingWave is an event streaming platform for agentic AI. It continuously ingests data from databases, event streams, and webhooks, processes it incrementally, and serves fresh results at low latency, replacing the traditional event streaming stack (e.g., Debezium + Kafka + Flink + serving DB) with a single system."],"features":["Monitoring and alerting: continuous evaluation of streaming metrics against thresholds","Feature stores: batch and streaming features computed over the same pipeline, served from the same system","Live dashboards: materialized views updated incrementally, no scheduled refreshes","Real-time enrichment: live events joined with historical reference data in-flight, before delivery downstream","Streaming lakehouses: continuous, exactly-once ingestion into open-format tables with automated compaction and snapshot management"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/risingwavelabs/risingwave/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"58b9d2e50c3a29bd9ea8188ea0893a0bd0c3c561a571440f0e79273a2904e6